{{!
    @template local_page/opengraph

    The Open Graph tags of a custom page - what a messaging app or social
    network reads when a link to the page is shared. Rendered into the document
    head by the before_standard_head_html_generation hook callback, which writes
    the name metas (description, keywords, author, robots) and the canonical
    link beside them as literal strings: the template lint validates a fragment
    as body content, where a meta carrying a name and a canonical link are
    invalid while RDFa property metas are not.

    Every value arrives in the PLAIN spelling and the double stashes escape it
    exactly once for the attribute. There is one title: the page's meta title,
    or its name when it has none. The description is optional: a page without
    a meta description gets no description tag at all. The image is optional
    too: it is served only for a published page, its address carries the
    file's content hash so that a replaced image is a new address, its alt text
    is the title, and its width and height are stated only when the file could
    be measured.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Fire & Rescue handbook",
        "hasdescription": true,
        "description": "Everything a new volunteer needs before the first shift.",
        "url": "https://moodle.example.org/local_page/category/7/handbook",
        "sitename": "Example Academy",
        "locale": "pt_BR",
        "hasimage": true,
        "imageurl": "https://moodle.example.org/pluginfile.php/42/local_page/ogimage/5/da39a3ee5e6b4b0d3255bfef95601890afd80709/cover.png",
        "imagetype": "image/png",
        "hasimagesize": true,
        "imagewidth": 1200,
        "imageheight": 630
    }
}}
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{title}}">
{{#hasdescription}}
<meta property="og:description" content="{{description}}">
{{/hasdescription}}
<meta property="og:url" content="{{url}}">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="{{sitename}}">
<meta property="og:locale" content="{{locale}}">
{{#hasimage}}
<meta property="og:image" content="{{imageurl}}">
<meta property="og:image:type" content="{{imagetype}}">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{title}}">
{{#hasimagesize}}
<meta property="og:image:width" content="{{imagewidth}}">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="{{imageheight}}">
{{/hasimagesize}}
{{/hasimage}}
